{% extends "base.mjml" %}
{% block content %}

{% macro bullet_list(items) %}
<mj-table>
  <tr>
    <td style="">
      <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="list" style width="100%">
        <tbody role="presentation">
          {% for item in items %}
          <tr>
            <td vertical-align="top">
              <ul role="presentation" class="list-item-wrap" align="left" type="disc" style="font-family:Verdana,Aerial; margin-left:25px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding:0;line-height:;">
                <li role="list-item" class="list-item" style="margin:0;padding:0;padding-left:3px;margin-bottom:3px;"> <span class="list-item__text" style="text-align:left;">{{ item }}</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
</mj-table>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro numbered_list(items) %}
<mj-table>
  <tr>
    <td style="">
      <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="list" style width="100%">
        <tbody role="presentation">
          {% for item in items %}
          <tr>
            <td vertical-align="top">
              <ol role="presentation" class="list-item-wrap" align="left" type="1" style="font-family:Verdana,Aerial; margin-left:25px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding:0;line-height:;">
                <li role="list-item" class="list-item" style="margin:0;padding:0;padding-left:3px;margin-bottom:3px;"> <span class="list-item__text" style="text-align:left;">{{ item }}</span>
                </li>
              </ol>
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
</mj-table>
{% endmacro %}

<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text>
      PyConZA 2026 starts this Wednesday! Here's everything you need before
      you arrive.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2">Getting there and parking</mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Beginners' Day (14 Oct) and the talks (15-16 Oct) take place at
      <a href="https://www.belmontsquare.co.za/">J&J Conferences</a> at
      Belmont Square in Rondebosch.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Extra parking is available at the nearby
      <strong>Rygersdal Sports Club</strong>. On Thursday and Friday, a
      shuttle will run between the parking and the venue.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-button mj-class="action-button" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/oTSryhXFmbuY5xs86"
      >Get directions</mj-button
    >
    <mj-button
      mj-class="action-button"
      href="https://za.pycon.org/pages/venue/in_person_venue/"
      >Venue details</mj-button
    >
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2">Register on Discord</mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Discord is our home base for the conference, whether you're joining in
      person or online. This is where you'll find announcements, talk
      discussions and speaker Q&A, and where you'll register for the Meet and
      Greet (see below).
    </mj-text>
    {{ numbered_list([
      "<strong>Join the PyConZA Discord</strong> using the button below.",
      "<strong>Register with the bot.</strong> The bot will send you a direct message. Reply in that message with <code>!register</code> followed by your Quicket ticket barcode number. Send just the number.",
      "<strong>You're in.</strong> The bot checks your ticket, unlocks the conference channels, and sets your nickname to the name on your ticket.",
    ]) }}
    <mj-text>
      <strong>Good to know:</strong>
    </mj-text>
    {{ bullet_list([
      "Register in the bot's direct message, not in a public channel, so your barcode stays private.",
      "The PyConZA 2026 channels stay hidden until the conference opens, so don't worry if you can't see them yet.",
      "If the bot can't find your ticket, ask for help in #helpdesk.",
      "During talks, type <code>!question</code> followed by your question in that talk's channel to send it to the speaker.",
    ]) }}
    <mj-button mj-class="action-button" href="https://discord.gg/8R875rbS48"
      >Join Discord</mj-button
    >
    <mj-button
      mj-class="action-button"
      href="https://za.pycon.org/pages/venue/remote_venue/"
      >Discord guide</mj-button
    >
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2">Beginners' Day: Wednesday 14 October</mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      We're planning to start at <strong>9:00</strong> (still tentative, so
      watch #announcements on Discord for updates).
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      <strong>Bring your laptop!</strong> You don't need any experience or
      anything installed in advance. Our mentors will help you get set up on
      the day. Remember that your R50 is refunded when you attend.
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2">Meet and Greet: Wednesday evening</mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Join us on Wednesday evening (venue and time to be confirmed) to meet
      other attendees, speakers and organisers before the talks begin.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      If you'd like to come, register on Discord (see above) and join the
      <a href="https://discord.com/channels/738062950316900393/1559290011600551976"
        ><strong>PyConZA Hallway → Outings → Meet-and-greet, 2026</strong></a
      >
      forum post. You'll find the details there, and it's how you let us know
      you're coming so we can make the booking.
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2">The schedule is live</mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      The full schedule for Thursday and Friday is now up, so you can plan
      which talks you'd like to see. Registration opens at 08:30 on Thursday,
      and the welcome starts at 09:00. Some changes may still be made, so
      check the schedule on the day for the latest times and rooms.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-button mj-class="action-button" href="https://za.pycon.org/schedule/"
      >View the schedule</mj-button
    >
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2"
      >Sign up for sprints: Saturday 17 and Sunday 18 October</mj-text
    >
    <mj-text>
      We've found a sprint venue! The sprints will be held at UCT Department
      of Computer Science Senior Laboratory, from 08:30 to 17:00 each day.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Sprints are a chance to work on open-source projects with other
      developers, and you don't need to be an expert to join in. Sprints are
      included with your conference ticket. Please sign up so we know how many
      people to expect.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-button mj-class="action-button" href="https://forms.gle/LKtPJhNsX7wWoNbW6"
      >Sign up for sprints</mj-button
    >
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-section mj-class="body-section">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text mj-class="heading-2"
      >Bring something for the Maker's Room</mj-text
    >
    <mj-text>
      Have you made something you'd like to show off, or do you have a tool
      you use to make things? Bring it along! The Maker's Room is open
      throughout the conference. Anyone can display their things there, and no
      registration is needed. The room is locked after hours for security.
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text> See you soon! </mj-text>
    <mj-text>
      Best regards,
      <br />
      The PyConZA committee
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

{% endblock content %}
